<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Harry Nkumbula</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1916">1916</a>–<a href="/years/1983">1983</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Harry Nkumbula was a Zambian nationalist who led the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/northern-rhodesia">Northern Rhodesia</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/african-national-congress">African National Congress</a> from 1951 and campaigned against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/federation-of-rhodesia-and-nyasaland">Federation of Rhodesia and Nyasaland</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kenneth-kaunda">Kenneth Kaunda</a> and other younger leaders broke away from him in 1958, and their movement soon became the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-national-independence-party">United National Independence Party</a>. Nkumbula's congress joined a coalition government in 1962, and he remained the main opposition leader until <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zambia">Zambia</a> became a one-party state in 1972.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/harry-nkumbula.jpg" alt="Harry Nkumbula" width="228" height="256" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Times of Zambia · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Harry_Nkumbula.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
